# Tech stack & engineering rules

## Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 14 (Pages Router) with **`output: "export"`** —
  the site is fully statically pre-rendered to `out/` and served from
  GitHub Pages at `haque-consulting.com`.
- **Language**: TypeScript strict mode.
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS only. No CSS-in-JS, no SCSS, no inline `style`
  attributes for layout.
- **Animation**: `framer-motion` only. No `animejs`, no GSAP, no canvas.
- **Icons**: `lucide-react` only.
- **SEO**: `next-seo` for meta + JSON-LD inline on home page.
- **Fonts**: `next/font/google` (self-hosted at build time). Never re-add a
  `<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/...">`.
- **Deploy**: GitHub Actions → GitHub Pages (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`).
  `public/CNAME` declares the custom domain.

## Forbidden libraries

Do not reintroduce any of these without an explicit ticket:

- `three`, `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei` (heavy, no use case here).
- `animejs` (we use framer-motion).
- Carousel libraries (`swiper`, `keen-slider`, `react-slick`, etc.).
- jQuery or any DOM-manipulating runtime.
- Any analytics package without consent handling.

## Code style

- 2-space indent, TypeScript everywhere, no `any` unless commented why.
- Components are functions, default-exported, named PascalCase.
- File names match component names (`Hero.tsx` exports `Hero`).
- Keep components dumb; lift logic to hooks if it grows.
- No comments that just narrate code (“// loop over items”). Comments only
  for non-obvious intent or constraints.
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` before opening a PR; both must
  pass cleanly with **zero warnings**.

## Performance budget

Hard limits for the home page on a mid-tier mobile (Moto G4 / 4G):

- LCP **< 2.5 s**
- CLS **< 0.1**
- INP **< 200 ms**
- Total JS shipped on first load: **< 150 kB gzip**.
- No render-blocking third-party requests on first paint.
- Below-the-fold images **must** be lazy.
- Any new dependency over ~30 kB needs justification.

## Static export caveats (don’t break these)

- `next/image` must keep `images.unoptimized: true` (Pages can’t optimize).
- No `getServerSideProps`, no API routes — they fail static export.
- Any new page goes in `pages/` (Pages Router), not `app/`.
- Keep `trailingSlash: true` so `/foo/` → `/foo/index.html` works on Pages.

## Adding pages

Currently a single-page site with anchor sections. If a real
multi-page split is needed (e.g. `/case-studies/[slug]`), each new route
must be statically generable (`getStaticProps` + `getStaticPaths` with
`fallback: false`).
